From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:53:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: uniform texture handles (NAK_TEX_UHANDLE),
 occupancy-target knobs

NAK_TEX_UHANDLE (default off, SM100+): a bindless texture handle that is
the same in every lane (by NIR's divergence analysis of the texture and
sampler parts) goes in the uniform register field of TEX, TLD and TLD4
(opcodes 0xf60, 0xf66, 0xf63) instead of the second source vector, as
in the reference compiler's code.  The second vector is then often
empty, and the sources use the scalar form (.SCR) without the copies
that build contiguous vectors.  Legalization brings the handle back to
a UGPR with R2UR if NAK moved it to a GPR.

NAK_REMAT_LD_COST (1-63, default 4): what a rematerialized load costs in
the spiller and in the occupancy target's dry run.  NAK_OCC_GPRS (0-255,
default off): a fixed register target for every shader whose natural
count is higher, for sweeps of one shader with dispatch-replay.

All three are in nak_knobs_key2(), so in NVK's pipeline cache keys.
